WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:05.204
-Hello, everyone, and welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:06.973
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:08.074
Thank you very much.

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:09.609
Well, guys,
I want to say congrats to

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:13.880
the Tampa Bay Buccaneers
on winning Super Bowl LV.

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:16.282
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:18.584
What a weekend
for the people of Tampa.

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:22.321
48 hours of nonstop drinking and
partying in the streets

00:00:22.354 --> 00:00:25.191
and then the Super Bowl.

00:00:25.224 --> 00:00:26.959
Yeah, they partied hard
in Tampa.

00:00:26.992 --> 00:00:28.127
One girl was so drunk,

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.798
she made out with the
Vince Lombardi hologram.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.534
That's right -- Tampa Bay
blew out the Kansas City Chiefs.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.537
The final score was
Chiefs 9, Bucs 31,

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:41.641
Paramount+ commercials 12,000.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.242
Yeah, the game
was over pretty early.

00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:45.445
For the people of
Tampa, that was a great night.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.579
For the rest of the country,

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:49.282
it was a ZzzQuil injection.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.551
Yep, it wasn't
the most suspenseful game.

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.953
The most exciting part of
the night was Bruce Springsteen

00:00:53.986 --> 00:00:56.756
wandering around
a town in Kansas.

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:58.991
At a certain point,
even Buccaneers fans were like,

00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:00.893
"Just end the game
so we can get to Queen Latifah.

00:01:00.926 --> 00:01:02.862
Come on. That show looks good.

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:04.630
It's a good show, by the way.
-Yeah.

00:01:04.663 --> 00:01:06.099
-Seriously,
the game was such a dud,

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:07.233
I watched it from home

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:13.372
and I still left early
to beat traffic.

00:01:13.405 --> 00:01:15.942
But the big story, of course,
is that Tom Brady

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:20.814
won his seventh championship
and fifth Super Bowl MVP.

00:01:22.414 --> 00:01:24.417
Can we see Tom Brady
after the game?

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.386
Yeah. He just played
four hours of football

00:01:27.419 --> 00:01:30.923
and he looks like
he's about to go to a wedding.

00:01:30.956 --> 00:01:32.892
Yeah, Brady has
cemented his place on

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:34.193
the sports Mount Rushmore,

00:01:34.226 --> 00:01:36.462
alongside Michael Jordan,
Muhammad Ali,

00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:38.064
and that fan who took
a home-run ball

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:40.967
to the chest to save his beers.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.469
That guy's a Bud Light
legend right there.

00:01:43.502 --> 00:01:46.172
That was like, "Oof!"

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:47.373
Meanwhile, last night's game was

00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:49.008
tough to watch
for Patriots fans.

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:51.410
Right now, there are 2-year-olds
in Boston going,

00:01:51.443 --> 00:01:54.547
"When will this
championship drought end?"

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:57.083
Yep, today in Boston,
fans are happy for Brady,

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:58.718
but sad that
he left the Patriots,

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:01.020
which probably explains
Sam Adams' new beer,

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:04.624
Sam Adams Bittahsweet Teahhs.

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:09.362
Bittahsweet Teahhs.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:12.431
Of course, Tom Brady's longtime
teammate Rob Gronkowski

00:02:12.464 --> 00:02:15.268
also had a great game,
scoring the first two touchdowns

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.770
and winning his
fourth Super Bowl.

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:20.506
Yep, "Gronk" scored two
touchdowns in the first half.

00:02:20.539 --> 00:02:22.975
He would have had more, but he
spent the whole second half

00:02:23.008 --> 00:02:27.513
stuck in The Weeknd's
house of mirrors.

00:02:27.546 --> 00:02:28.781
Yeah, a lot of people
were talking about

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:30.683
The Weeknd's
halftime performance.

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:33.719
In case you missed it,
grab a Dramamine and enjoy.

00:02:33.752 --> 00:02:37.957
-♪ She told me,
"Don't worry about it" ♪

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:41.827
♪ She told me to worry no more ♪
-Okay. Okay.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.030
Well, if anyone's
missed the feeling of

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.331
being drunk on a cruise,

00:02:45.364 --> 00:02:48.167
this was a nice walk down
memory lane.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.137
Yep, The Weeknd performed inside
a gold house of mirrors.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:54.240
You know, I've never
been to Mar-a-Lago, but...

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:59.245
Meanwhile, I read that over
16 million Americans were

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:01.814
expected to miss work today
because of the Super Bowl.

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:04.617
16 million.
Tariq, do you believe that?

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:08.821
-Ha ha ha! That's crazy.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.925
-Tariq, something
different about you today?

00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:16.362
-Ha ha ha! That's crazy.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:21.567
-Maybe you went a little hard
watching the game last night?

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:25.771
-Ha ha ha! That's crazy.

00:03:25.804 --> 00:03:28.241
-Or maybe you got this
giant cutout of yourself

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:30.543
and just pre-recorded yourself
saying something vague,

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:33.947
like "Ha ha ha, that's crazy"
and skipped work today.

00:03:35.247 --> 00:03:38.851
-Ha ha ha! That's crazy.

00:03:38.884 --> 00:03:42.755
-Alright, let's just move on.

00:03:42.788 --> 00:03:44.490
Well, before kickoff,
President Biden

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:46.726
was interviewed on CBS,
and he talked about how

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:49.395
he used to dream about
playing in the NFL.

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:52.732
But the position he mentioned
sounded a little dated.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.000
Watch this.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.235
-So, many people may not know
that you were once

00:03:56.268 --> 00:03:58.971
a pretty good receiver
yourself back in the day.

00:03:59.004 --> 00:04:01.007
-I had wild dreams.
It wasn't to be president.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.909
I thought I could be
a flanker back in the NFL.

00:04:03.942 --> 00:04:08.681
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:11.384
-Huh?

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:14.287
Flanker back?

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.655
Kind of crazy
that our new president

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:17.223
is older than the forward pass.

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:19.158
Isn't that wild?

00:04:19.191 --> 00:04:23.195
Even the Vince Lombardi hologram
was like, "How old is this guy?"

00:04:23.228 --> 00:04:24.563
Biden was like,
"Just like every kid,

00:04:24.596 --> 00:04:28.234
I wanted to be a flanker back
for the NFL's top team,

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:32.104
the Delaware Dirt Devils,

00:04:32.137 --> 00:04:35.941
under coach Peppy Lagraine.

00:04:35.974 --> 00:04:38.911
He had one arm
and three nipples."

00:04:41.513 --> 00:04:42.815
Get this.

00:04:42.848 --> 00:04:44.850
I heard that, in Russia,
they're offering free ice cream

00:04:44.883 --> 00:04:48.487
as an incentive to get
a COVID-19 vaccine.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:51.490
Yeah, that's what everyone
in Russia wants in February --

00:04:51.523 --> 00:04:54.260
ice cream.

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:56.362
Putin even came up with
a catchy jingle for it.

00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:58.898
[ Russian accent ] "I scream,
you scream, we all scream

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:01.634
'cause I poison
your underpants."

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:05.871
[ Normal voice ]
"What did you say?"

00:05:05.904 --> 00:05:07.006
Well, this is fun.

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:08.941
Serving the ice cream is
the Russian version

00:05:08.974 --> 00:05:12.278
of Ben and Jerry,
Bogdan and Yuri.

00:05:12.311 --> 00:05:13.813
Officials were like,
"It's fresh.

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:17.350
It comes from milk of bears."

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:18.784
Some TV news.

00:05:18.817 --> 00:05:21.987
Well, guys, after being named in
a multi-billion-dollar lawsuit

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:24.690
for spreading false claims
of election fraud,

00:05:24.723 --> 00:05:28.094
Fox Business has canceled
"Lou Dobbs Tonight."

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.096
You know, there's a clip that
we like to show sometimes

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:34.600
where Lou Dobbs mispronounces
the name of a Mexican town.

00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:35.901
Here, take a look.

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:39.271 line:0%
-The caravan of mostly
Central American immigrants

00:05:39.304 --> 00:05:42.408 line:0%
is now in the Mexican City
of "Wa-kla-da."

00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:45.244
-Yeah.

00:05:47.312 --> 00:05:48.347
That's right.

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.216
Well, out of respect,
we will no longer

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:51.817
show that clip on
"The Tonight Show."

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.252
We're retiring it.

00:05:53.285 --> 00:05:55.955
But just in case you forgot
which clip I'm talking about,

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:58.357
here it is one more time.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:00.826 line:0%
-...the Mexican City
of "Wa-kla-da."

00:06:00.859 --> 00:06:03.596
-To clarify, we will not show

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:06.332
this clip on our show anymore.

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:07.666 line:0%
-..."Wa-kla-da."

00:06:07.699 --> 00:06:13.105
-That's right -- we will never
show that clip again.

00:06:13.138 --> 00:06:14.573
That clip being...

00:06:14.606 --> 00:06:16.976 line:0%
-...the Mexican City
of "Wa-kla-da."

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:22.081
-Farewell, Lou Dobbs.
We hardly knew ye.

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:23.916
And, finally, I heard about
a Massachusetts man

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:25.985
who got some interesting news
at the hospital.

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:27.119
Listen to this.

00:06:27.152 --> 00:06:29.789 line:0%
-A Massachusetts man
who suddenly woke up

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:32.992 line:0%
struggling to breathe was
stunned when doctors told him

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:37.063 line:0%
he had swallowed one of
his AirPods in his sleep.

00:06:39.264 --> 00:06:40.900
-He only realized it
when his stomach

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:44.236
started singing
"Drivers License."

00:06:44.269 --> 00:06:45.738
He also had a tough time hearing

00:06:45.771 --> 00:06:47.807
'cause of the two Tic Tacs
shoved in his ears.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.240
We have a great show.

